How to Run the Project

1. Download the repository.
2. Open the Gym Management System folder.
3. Make sure the data folder is located inside the project folder where all the python programs are.
4. Run the interactive.py file.

Example:
python interactive.py
The main menu will then be displayed:

--- Gym Management System ---
1. Member Management
2. Trainer Management
3. Workout Plan Management
4. Payment Management
5. Exit

---

# Gym management System

Project Report

The complete project report is available in the repository:

Path: 'Gisma/B100A Python Programming WS0926'

A simple Gym Management System developed using Python as part of a Bachelor's programming project at Gisma University of Applied Sciences.

The purpose of this project is to create a simple management system that can store and manage information about gym members, trainers, workout plans and payments.

---

Member Management
Functions include:

Register a new member
View all members
Search for a member
Update member contact information
Assign a trainer to a member

Example information includes:
Member ID
Member name
Email
Phone number
Assigned trainer
Trainer Management

Functions include:
Add a trainer
View trainers
Assign members to trainers
View the number of clients assigned to a trainer

Example information includes:
Trainer ID
Trainer name
Assigned clients
Workout Plan Management

Functions include:
Create a workout plan
Add exercises
View workout plans
Update workout difficulty
Remove exercises

Example information includes:

Plan ID
Plan name
Difficulty level
Exercises
Payment Management

Functions include:
Record a payment
View payments
Check payment status
Mark payments as completed or failed
Update payment amounts

Example information includes:

Payment ID
Member ID
Payment amount
Payment status

---

The project demonstrates the use of Python programming concepts including:

Classes and objects
Functions and methods
Dictionaries
Lists
Loops and conditional statements
CSV file handling
Basic exception handling
Modular programming

The project demonstrates the development of a simple real-world Gym Management System using Python.
